---
description: Keep each track of work organized in git
alwaysApply: true
---

Keep each track of work recognizable in its branch, commits, and pull request.

- Stay on the current branch when this chat belongs to that track.
- When the checkout has another conversation's changes, or this chat is a different track, ask before mixing them. Separate with a new branch, separate commits, or by leaving the other work untouched.
- Never commit directly to the integration branch (default `main`) or the production branch.
- Branch from the integration branch and open pull requests into it.
- Never push or open a pull request unless asked in that turn. Invoking `/pr` is that ask — follow `Agents/skills/pr/SKILL.md`.

Branch naming, commit style, and worktrees live in `Agents/context/git-workflow.md`. Read it before creating a branch or committing.
